  "authoringDirection": "Whole surviving Fort Lytton: actual pentagonal main earthworks/open grassy court/moat/causeway and entry passage, northern and northwestern casemates with seven gun positions and defining restored artillery, engine-room/coal-store corner, two mapped southern/eastern brick stores and surviving concrete slabs. Western battery/pits5and6, WWII searchlight and command-post remnants, bounded gun-cotton-store/priming-pit ruins and1903 searchlight/old jetty/winch-block traces where primary relative information supports them. Neighbouring Lytton Quarantine Station/chimney/refinery, museum display collections unrelated to fixed positions, modern shelters/movie-set remnants/picnic equipment/boats/trees/people/inscriptions excluded.",
